{"parentUuid":"dbaff355-c6b6-48dc-9679-4af70bdde1b1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eea1a00a-fa8d-4ce0-963d-d0f411062aaf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015exj6jYSVCjihS1rEASy5i","type":"tool_result","content":"# How Soul ID Works\n\n## Photo Upload Requirements\n\nTo begin, creators need to supply approximately **20+ clear, well-lit reference images** showing different angles and expressions. The system accepts up to 80 photos total. For optimal results, maintain a resolution of \"960px or higher per photo for best quality.\" Avoid sunglasses, masks, or extreme expressions, as these reduce reference data quality.\n\n## Character Creation and Training\n\nOnce photos are uploaded, the training process takes \"3 to 5 minutes\" and costs 25 credits (approximately $1.25). Rather than simply matching a single reference image, Soul ID builds an internalized model. The system analyzes facial structure, hair, posture, and expression patterns to create a digital twin that understands the person's core identity rather than copying a snapshot.\n\n## Reuse Across Content\n\nA trained Soul ID avatar can be deployed across both image and video generation indefinitely. The same identity applies automatically to every project without retraining. Creators select from \"20+ built-in looks (editorial, retro, Y2K, and more)\" style presets to define tone while maintaining character consistency.\n\n## UI Steps\n\nThe process follows this workflow:\n1. Upload reference photos\n2. Train the avatar (system processes the images)\n3. Select style presets\n4. Generate content using the avatar\n5. Reuse and scale across platforms"}]},"uuid":"1b966ae3-2f40-4c81-95d7-c7f7bf62d12d","timestamp":"2026-09-21T01:17:59.142Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":26982,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# How Soul ID Works\n\n## Photo Upload Requirements\n\nTo begin, creators need to supply approximately **20+ clear, well-lit reference images** show